    <string name="onboarding_home_title">Set as Home</string>
    <string name="onboarding_home_body">Make XR Launcher the default Home app so it opens when you press Home and when glasses connect. You can change this later in Android settings.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_show_again">How to use XR Launcher</string>
    <string name="onboarding_welcome_title">A launcher for XR</string>
    <string name="onboarding_welcome_body">XR Launcher is a spatial HOME for Android XR glasses and large screens. Your phone is the controller when the workspace is on glasses.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_phone_title">Phone HOME</string>
    <string name="onboarding_phone_body">Use this screen like any launcher — search, tap an app, or pin favorites in the dock. Settings and this intro live in the top-right.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_connect_title">Connect glasses</string>
    <string name="onboarding_connect_body">Plug in or pair your XR glasses so Android treats them as a second display. When they appear, tap Control glasses on the dock.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_touchpad_title">Touchpad controls</string>
    <string name="onboarding_touchpad_body">Control glasses opens the spatial workspace on the XR display and a touchpad on the phone. Drag to move the cursor; use Left / Right click for taps.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_accessibility_title">Desktop pointer</string>
    <string name="onboarding_accessibility_body">Enable Settings → Accessibility → XR Launcher display pointer so clicks work over other apps on the glasses display, not only the launcher.</string>
